                <pb facs="0357" n="267" sameAs="frus:frus1934v03/pg267"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77 Chinese Eastern/1326: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bullitt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-09-02T18:00:00+03:00">September 2, 1934—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 2—5:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>282. The Japanese Embassy here insists that the Russians have reopened
                    negotiations for the sale of the Chinese Eastern Railroad and that Soviet
                    reports of Japanese threats to seize the railroad are groundless and designed to
                    arouse sympathy in the United States.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bullitt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
